Fix: Set TraceEnable Off in the server configuration.
References: Apache Module core (TraceEnable)
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST CM-6, CM-7; ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

TRACE requests are answered: TraceEnable is On in the file and line
named, or nowhere set, and the default is On for the 2.x server. A
TRACE answer echoes the request back, which aids cross-site tracing
attacks. Set TraceEnable Off.
